
Languages:

HTML    	app/src/index.html — the app's layout (sidebar, tabs, toolbar, settings panel)
CSS	      app/src/css/glass.css and app.css — the frosted-glass look, colors, layout
JavaScript	    app/src/js/app.js and settings.js — tabs, navigation, the ⌘K command menu, the Google→Geo swap logic
Rust	          app/src-tauri/src/main.rs — the native desktop shell; creates each tab as a real OS-level webview
TOML	          app/src-tauri/Cargo.toml — Rust's package/dependency file
JSON	          app/package.json and app/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json — npm config and app/window settings

Frameworks & tools

Tauri (v2)	The core framework — wraps your HTML/CSS/JS frontend in a real native desktop app, and lets main.rs create/control native browser tabs

Node.js       / npm	Runs your build scripts (npm run dev, npm run build, npm run icon)
Cargo	Rust's package manager —       compiles main.rs and all the Rust dependencies (this is what you saw compiling in your terminal output)
serde /             serde_json (Rust crates)	Used by the Rust side for reading/writing structured data (config, messages between JS and Rust)
